.DS_Store
fhirpkg.lock.json
Thumbs.db
# Everything under input-cache is transient EXCEPT the terminology cache:
# committed txcache makes CI render the same ValueSet expansions the local
# Ontoserver-backed build produced (publisher consults the cache BEFORE the
# server), while the PACKAGE stays intensional (expansions never enter
# fsh-generated or the package build).
/input-cache/*
!/input-cache/txcache/
/out
/output
/temp
/template
validator_cli.jar

# --- merged from mii-kds-module-template v0.13.1 (.gitignore; fsh-generated/ line dropped: this module COMMITS fsh-generated per org CI convention) ---
# --- IG Publisher / SUSHI build artifacts (regenerated on every build) ---
# The generated IG website. Never commit it; previews are published via CI.
output/
# IG Publisher scratch space.
temp/
# The template package the IG Publisher extracts into ./template at build
# time. Why: this repo REFERENCES the template in ig.ini (repository URL today,
# package pin once published); the extracted copy is a build artifact. (The
# deliberate vendored fallback copy lives under a different, tracked path:
# ig-template/.)
template/
# Downloaded FHIR package cache.
# FSH -> FHIR JSON output generated by SUSHI.
# The IG Publisher jar itself — downloaded, version-pinned, never committed.
publisher.jar

# --- Tooling ---
node_modules/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
*.log

# The migration run log and its per-step raw logs are EVIDENCE, committed
# with the branch (skill mii-ig-migration, run-log contract) — exempt from the
# *.log noise rule above.
!migration-log/*.log
!migration-log/*.prev.log
# The IG Publisher's translation working directory at the repo ROOT (not
# input/translations!) — build scratch, never committed.
/translations/
